### Health check — sanity-check the app is up
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

### OpenAPI document — full machine-readable contract
GET http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs

### Chat: helper personality (no sessionId — server generates one)
# The "client.global.set" line captures the returned sessionId into a variable
# named `sessionId` so the next request can reuse it.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personality": "helper",
  "message": "What is polymorphism? Keep it under 50 words."
}

> {%
client.global.set("sessionId", response.body.sessionId);
client.log("Captured sessionId: " + response.body.sessionId);
%}

### Follow-up in the SAME session — verifies memory works
# Sends the sessionId captured above. The model should answer as if it saw
# the previous question, e.g. "you mean about polymorphism?".
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personality": "helper",
  "message": "Can you give me a one-line Java example of it?",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
}

### Chat: pirate personality
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personality": "pirate",
  "message": "How do I find the nearest port?"
}

### Chat: coder personality
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personality": "coder",
  "message": "Show me a Java 21 record that models a 2D point with a distance method."
}

### Validation error: missing required `message` field -> 400 problem+json
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personality": "helper"
}

### Validation error: blank `personality` -> 400 problem+json
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personality": "",
  "message": "Hi"
}

### Unknown personality -> 400 with "requestedPersonality" property
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personality": "villain",
  "message": "Hi"
}

### Continue an existing conversation by hand — set sessionId to one you've seen
# Replace the value below with a sessionId from a previous response.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personality": "helper",
  "message": "What did I ask earlier?",
  "sessionId": "paste-a-real-session-id-here"
}
